From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:58:07 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: pmp: Keep power commands after an unhandled
 message on other boards

Any error from handling a PMP message now goes through fail_display(),
which also latches the device-power command stream as failed. On T8140,
T6041 and the other PMP boards, one unknown opcode or one failed reply
then makes every later apple_pmp_set_device_power() return -EIO,
including the DCP display vote. Before, the error was only logged.

Latch the failure only on the retained J713 bridge, which needs it, and
keep logging the error on every board.

Fixes: 1ae4d49f3592 ("soc: apple: expose retained PMP display and GPU ownership")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit 444c52644826e99eecf65e9f643744c9e380bca9)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/pmp.rs | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/pmp.rs b/drivers/soc/apple/pmp.rs
index 666aea5976..2e069a34f4 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/pmp.rs
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/pmp.rs
@@ -593,7 +593,12 @@ impl rtkit::Operations for PmpData {
     fn recv_message(data: <Self::Data as ForeignOwnable>::Borrowed<'_>, _ep: u8, msg: u64) {
         let ret = data.recv_message(msg);
         if let Err(e) = ret {
-            data.fail_display(e);
+            // Only the retained J713 bridge latches a message it cannot
+            // handle as fatal. Other boards log it and keep power commands.
+            // SAFETY: read-only board identity check.
+            if unsafe { bindings::apple_pmp_display_retained_board() } {
+                data.fail_display(e);
+            }
             dev_err!(data.dev, "Failed to handle rtkit message, error: {:?}", e);
         }
     }
